<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1958</h1><p class="ref-lede">1958 in world history: 31 events, 5 births, 12 deaths, 4 works, 6 states founded and 17 that came to an end. 344 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1954">1954</a><a href="/years/1955">1955</a><a href="/years/1956">1956</a><a href="/years/1957">1957</a><a href="/years/1958" aria-current="page">1958</a><a href="/years/1959">1959</a><a href="/years/1960">1960</a><a href="/years/1961">1961</a><a href="/years/1962">1962</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-1">1 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The European Economic Community comes into being</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-rome">Treaty of Rome</a> took effect, creating a common market among <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-germany">West Germany</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luxembourg">Luxembourg</a>. The EEC was the forerunner of today's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-4">4 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Sputnik 1 falls from orbit</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The first artificial satellite burned up in the atmosphere after three months and some 1,400 orbits. Its launch the previous October had shocked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and started the space race.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/boston" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boston.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-18">18 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Willie O'Ree breaks the NHL colour barrier</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Playing for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a> Bruins against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montreal">Montreal</a> Canadiens, Willie O'Ree became the first Black player in the National Hockey League, despite being almost blind in one eye.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-31">31 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Explorer 1, America's first satellite, is launched</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A Jupiter-C rocket put Explorer 1 into orbit from Cape Canaveral, four months after Sputnik. Its Geiger counter detected the Van Allen radiation belts around the Earth.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-17">17 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">US launches Vanguard 1 satellite</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The grapefruit-sized satellite, mocked by Khrushchev, showed that the Earth is slightly pear-shaped. Long silent, it is the oldest human-made object still in orbit.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-14">14 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Iraqi army officers overthrow the Hashemite monarchy</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Officers led by Brigadier <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-karim-qasim">Abd al-Karim Qasim</a> seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> and killed King Faisal II and members of the royal family. The coup ended the British-backed monarchy and made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> a republic.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-29">29 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Eisenhower signs the act creating NASA</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Spurred by Sputnik, President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dwight-d-eisenhower">Eisenhower</a> signed the National Aeronautics and Space Act, creating a civilian space agency. NASA opened that October and within 11 years landed astronauts on the Moon.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-28">28 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Angelo Roncalli is elected Pope John XXIII</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The 76-year-old patriarch of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> was elected pope, widely seen as a caretaker. Within three months he announced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-vatican-council">Second Vatican Council</a>, which transformed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholic-church">Catholic Church</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-18">18 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The US launches SCORE, the first communications satellite</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">An <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlas-mountains">Atlas</a> rocket placed Project SCORE in orbit. The next day it broadcast a recorded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christmas">Christmas</a> message from President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dwight-d-eisenhower">Eisenhower</a>, the first voice transmitted from space.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/punto-fijo-pact" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/punto-fijo-pact.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/punto-fijo-pact">Punto Fijo Pact</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Punto Fijo Pact was an agreement signed on 31 October 1958 by Venezuela's main democratic parties, Democratic Action, COPEI and the Democratic Republican Union, after the fall of the dictator Marcos Pérez Jiménez.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/expo-58" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/expo-58.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/expo-58">Expo 58</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Expo 58 was the world's fair held in Brussels from April to October 1958, the first major international exposition after the Second World War.</p></div></li></ol></section>
